<title>VIETNAM: Vietnam to launch study for aluminium plant - paper.</title>
<headline>Vietnam to launch study for aluminium plant - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam's prime minister has approved a prefeasibility study for the construction of an aluminium plant with annual output of 150,000 to 200,000 tonnes of alumina and 75,000 tonnes of aluminium, a newspaper report said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The twice-weekly Vietnam Economic Times said the plant, in the southern central highlands province of Lam Dong, would use bauxite from a local mine which has reserves of 300 million tonnes.</p>
<p>It said domestic capital would be used to finance the $400 million plant. No target date for completion of the project was given.</p>
</text>
